@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+# Lending library
+
+A small web service of a lending library. A member reads the loans they hold and the fines they owe at `GET /members/{memberId}/loans`.
+
+- Java 17, Spring Boot 3.3.5 with Spring Web, and JUnit 5 with Spring Boot Test.
+- The application lives under `org.example.library`. The module `loan` follows the hexagonal layout: `app/api` holds what the module offers, `app/spi` what it needs, `app/domain` the business rules, `in/web` the web entry, `out/memory` the stores, and `config` the wiring.
+- The stores keep their data in memory, so the service needs no database.
+- The mail library Postbox is vendored under `vendor/postbox/`, at the version and the edition that its README names. The build compiles it as a second main source folder.
+
+## Build
+
+Gradle 9.8.1 builds the service with the default JDK, with no network:
+
+```bash
+gradle --offline test
+```
+
+The integration tests start the application and call its web entry through `MockMvc`.
